1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,300
Expressions Using Letter Numbers.

2
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:08,174
Think about traffic lights — they cycle through red, amber, and

3
00:00:08,274 --> 00:00:11,926
green, then repeat. If someone asks what colour is showing at

4
00:00:12,026 --> 00:00:15,678
the fortieth change, you would not count all forty. You would

5
00:00:15,778 --> 00:00:18,508
spot the repeating cycle, and use it cleverly.

6
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:25,907
A repeating pattern cycles through a fixed set of elements before starting

7
00:00:26,007 --> 00:00:30,656
again. The number of elements in one complete cycle is called the

8
00:00:30,756 --> 00:00:35,260
cycle length. For the traffic light, the cycle length is three.

9
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:41,770
To find which element appears at position n, we divide n by the cycle

10
00:00:41,870 --> 00:00:46,899
length, and look at the remainder. The remainder tells us exactly where we are

11
00:00:46,999 --> 00:00:51,831
within the current cycle. A remainder of one points to the first element, a

12
00:00:51,931 --> 00:00:56,302
remainder of two to the second, and so on. If the remainder is zero,

13
00:00:56,402 --> 00:00:59,985
we have landed exactly on the last element of the cycle.

14
00:01:02,866 --> 00:01:06,782
For the traffic light — position forty. Divide forty by

15
00:01:06,882 --> 00:01:11,310
three. Forty divided by three gives thirteen, with a remainder

16
00:01:11,410 --> 00:01:14,742
of one. Remainder one means we are at the first

17
00:01:14,842 --> 00:01:18,174
element — red. The fortieth position shows red.

18
00:01:20,333 --> 00:01:23,813
A pattern repeats — circle, square, triangle —

19
00:01:23,913 --> 00:01:28,249
then repeats. What shape appears at position twenty-nine?

20
00:01:29,866 --> 00:01:34,710
Cycle length is three. Divide twenty-nine by three — nine groups of

21
00:01:34,810 --> 00:01:39,948
three, with a remainder of two. Remainder two corresponds to the second

22
00:01:40,048 --> 00:01:44,670
element — square. The shape at position twenty-nine is a square.

23
00:01:47,133 --> 00:01:51,301
A repeating pattern cycles through a fixed set of elements before

24
00:01:51,401 --> 00:01:55,635
starting again. The remainder tells us exactly where we are within

25
00:01:55,735 --> 00:01:59,509
the current cycle. If the remainder is zero, we have landed

26
00:01:59,609 --> 00:02:02,201
exactly on the last element of the cycle.

